  "explanation": "Sequential toggles locate the experimental step that changes covariance. Global clock calibration and interactions travel with each switch, so this is not a unique causal allocation. Removing ability-dependent clock truncation can remove common pace covariance; fixed independent deadlines and score-dependent inbound/flight costs can still cause competitive clock coupling. Those microscopic explanations require separate experiments and are hypotheses, not proved by the switch table.",
